---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Accessibility Statement — JSDC Wheels">
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Accessibility Statement</h1>
    <p class="text-dark-400 mb-8">Last updated: May 6, 2025</p>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-dark-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">

      <div class="bg-dark-900 border border-dark-700/50 rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Our Commitment</h2>
        <p>
          JSDC Wheels is committed to making this website accessible to all users,
          including people with disabilities. We work to ensure our site meets or exceeds the
          requirements of the <em>Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act</em> (AODA)
          and targets conformance with the
          <strong class="text-white">Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.0 Level AA</strong>
          as the standard for our web presence.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Accessibility is an ongoing effort. We continually review and improve our website
          to reduce barriers and improve the experience for all visitors.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-dark-900 border border-dark-700/50 rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">AODA Compliance</h2>
        <p>
          As an Ontario business, JSDC Wheels is subject to the Accessibility for
          Ontarians with Disabilities Act, 2005 (AODA) and the Integrated Accessibility
          Standards Regulation (IASR). We are committed to:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-3 space-y-1 ml-2">
          <li>Providing accessible customer service</li>
          <li>Making our digital communications accessible</li>
          <li>Offering information in accessible formats upon request</li>
          <li>Ensuring our website meets WCAG 2.0 Level AA standards</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-dark-900 border border-dark-700/50 rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Accessibility Features</h2>
        <p>The following accessibility features are implemented on this website:</p>

        <h3 class="text-white font-medium mt-4 mb-2">Semantic HTML Structure</h3>
        <p>
          Pages use proper HTML5 semantic elements (<code class="text-primary-400">header</code>,
          <code class="text-primary-400">main</code>, <code class="text-primary-400">nav</code>,
          <code class="text-primary-400">footer</code>, <code class="text-primary-400">section</code>)
          to convey document structure to assistive technologies.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-white font-medium mt-4 mb-2">Keyboard Navigation</h3>
        <p>
          All interactive elements — links, buttons, form fields, and search controls — are
          reachable and operable using keyboard navigation alone. Focus states are visually
          indicated throughout the site.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-white font-medium mt-4 mb-2">Screen Reader Support</h3>
        <p>
          Interactive components include descriptive ARIA labels, roles, and states. Product
          cards, search results, and navigation elements are labeled to provide context to
          screen reader users beyond what is visually apparent.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-white font-medium mt-4 mb-2">Skip Navigation</h3>
        <p>
          A skip-to-main-content link is available at the top of each page, allowing keyboard
          and screen reader users to bypass the navigation header and jump directly to the
          main content.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-white font-medium mt-4 mb-2">Color Contrast</h3>
        <p>
          Text and interactive elements are designed to meet WCAG 2.0 AA contrast ratio
          requirements (minimum 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text). Information is
          not conveyed by color alone.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-white font-medium mt-4 mb-2">Responsive Design</h3>
        <p>
          The website is fully responsive and works across desktop, tablet, and mobile devices.
          Content reflows at all viewport sizes without horizontal scrolling. Text can be
          resized up to 200% without loss of content or functionality.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-white font-medium mt-4 mb-2">Image Alternatives</h3>
        <p>
          Product images include descriptive alt text. Decorative images use empty alt
          attributes so screen readers skip them appropriately. Where product images are
          unavailable, meaningful placeholder graphics with text descriptions are shown.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-white font-medium mt-4 mb-2">Form Accessibility</h3>
        <p>
          All form inputs have associated labels. Required fields are clearly indicated.
          Error messages are descriptive and programmatically associated with their inputs.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-dark-900 border border-dark-700/50 rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Known Limitations</h2>
        <p>
          While we strive for full WCAG 2.0 Level AA conformance, some areas are works in
          progress:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-3 space-y-1 ml-2">
          <li>
            The vehicle visualizer (third-party rendered images from IMAGIN.studio) may have
            limited accessibility for non-visual users. We provide vehicle specifications as
            text alongside the visualizer.
          </li>
          <li>
            Some dynamic search interactions may not announce results immediately to all
            screen reader software. We are reviewing these components for improvement.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-dark-900 border border-dark-700/50 rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Alternative Formats</h2>
        <p>
          If you need product information, pricing details, or any content from this website
          in an alternative format (such as large print, plain text, or another accessible
          format), please contact us and we will do our best to accommodate your request
          promptly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-dark-900 border border-dark-700/50 rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Feedback and Contact</h2>
        <p>
          We welcome feedback on the accessibility of our website. If you encounter any
          barriers, have difficulty accessing any content, or would like to request an
          accommodation or alternative format, please contact us:
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-1">
          <p><strong class="text-white">JSDC Wheels</strong></p>
          <p>Scarborough, Ontario, Canada</p>
          <p>
            Email:
            <a href="mailto:james@jsdcwheels.ca" class="text-primary-400 hover:underline">
              james@jsdcwheels.ca
            </a>
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Or use our <a href="/contact" class="text-primary-400 hover:underline">contact form</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We aim to respond to accessibility feedback within 5 business days.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-dark-900 border border-dark-700/50 rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Ongoing Improvements</h2>
        <p>
          Accessibility is not a one-time task. We conduct periodic reviews of our website
          against WCAG 2.0 Level AA criteria and address identified issues as part of our
          regular development cycle. Our commitment to accessibility is ongoing and we
          welcome reports from users who encounter barriers.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          This statement was prepared on May 6, 2025 and will be reviewed annually or when
          significant changes are made to the website.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
